{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: bounded implementation child of #20084 for the re-established 500,000-record checkpoint-restart miss. The scale-envelope campaign at harness head 0b689fe2 (retained evidence artifact git:sha1:510448fc1a5975989e2b73ae9e970cbf2d31a825, performance/retained/envelope-20260909-0b689fe2) measured cold restart from an authenticated tail-255 checkpoint at 500,000 records at 69.417 s and 69.320 s (diagnostic 69.784 s) on an 18-core Apple M5 Max with 64 GiB, every digest equal, load 2.67 to 4.40. That is still above the historical 60 s planning figure recorded with the earlier miss in #6231 (72.986 s average at retired b391c918), improved but not met. At 50,000 records the same restart takes 7.2 s, under the historical 10 s figure. The 60 s figure appears in no tracked contract and is not adopted, so nothing here is a broken commitment; the request recovers the miss as an outcome and leaves adoption to a proposal. Reconciliation before filing: no open assignment covers restart latency. The resident-memory outcome a9047812 is satisfied and covers status reads only; my earlier 47febbdb was withdrawn as its duplicate; a8d95f45 (#21817) is the bounded checkpoint decoder follow-up, a different outcome; the parked 8add6909 is the append fixed cost. The same run also observed 15.1 to 17.7 GiB peak RSS during checkpoint restart and cold verify at 500,000 with a 3.25 GB full-projection response; that is recorded separately as finding 53b0f429 with no target and is not a condition here, but any restart change should report its effect on it. Runtime optimisation was kept out of the evidence delivery by its conditions, which is why this is a separate request. Queue after your current promised work; the planner may reassign or retire this if a later durable owner is found.","body":{"branch":"request/checkpoint-restart-500k","conditions":"On request/checkpoint-restart-500k from then-current main, after the scale-envelope evidence delivery under #20084 has landed: reduce the cold restart from an authenticated tail-255 checkpoint at 500,000 records below the historical 60 s planning figure on the same hardware, or state with evidence why it cannot be met without a design change and what that change would be. Preserve complete verification and fold semantics, signed identities, correctness digests, checkpoint fallback behaviour, the 256 MiB checkpoint ceiling and every published lane. Measure with the existing performance framework's envelope tier under contract-v3 at the exact implementation head, two primary samples and one diagnostic, retained under performance/retained/ with raw samples, environment, digests and load log; no timing campaign in CI, no service restart, no change to governed limits without a proposal. Do not adopt the 60 s figure as a production commitment: that needs its own ordinary proposal; this request only recovers the miss. Independent Architecture/Security/Simplification review, ratified approval, sealed main merge, push, CI, worktree removal. Queue after your current promised work; the planner may reassign.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0b5fdd93443cedeef9dbc4ddf733d8c0b0bdd60d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:510448fc1a5975989e2b73ae9e970cbf2d31a825 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:00925ae6c09fb0b8e2a72e84c22ca3488bc9534d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:063ac469f4327eef88a6cef497d6b24b5d128af7, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:069ba281df08c36e7b19c66532ae24357887a9e5, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0953bfe693cd591ec4cd901025bc29c9047e27d2 and 61 more","target_head":"9fbc913e3fcc6bb2b28938fd8f189135dfe6c12e","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}